<% content_for :page_title, 'Session media' %><%= stylesheet_link_tag 'reservations' %><main class="lr-admin"><%= link_to '← Reservations', dashboard_reservations_path(site_id: @site.id), class: 'lr-link' %><header class="lr-hero"><div><span class="lr-eyebrow">LIGHTEK / TOGETHER</span><h1>Activate your session rooms.</h1><p>Voice, video, screen sharing and live audiences on your own server.</p></div></header><article class="lr-card" style="margin-top:24px"><h2><%= @site.name %></h2><p>Installation: <strong><%= @site.manifest.to_h.dig('session_media_install', 'status') || 'Not activated' %></strong></p><p>Install the managed LiveKit media service alongside this website. Lightek creates the credentials in Vault, configures the Docker service, connects HTTPS signaling through Apache, and opens the media ports. The Rails application keeps its current installation type.</p><p>The selected server needs Ubuntu, Apache with a working HTTPS virtual host, Docker support, and at least 2 GB RAM. Network requirements: TCP 7881, UDP 3478 and UDP 50000–50100. Provider firewalls must allow these ports too. Restricted corporate networks that require TURN over TLS/443 need a separately configured relay.</p><% if @installation %><%= button_to 'Install / verify session media', install_dashboard_session_media_path(site_id: @site.id, installation_id: @installation.id), class: 'lr-button', data: {turbo: false} %><% else %><p>Register this website’s installation in Servers & Applications before activating managed media.</p><% end %><p>This is a reusable installation action for each client server. No shared platform media credential is delivered to other client instances.</p></article></main>
